    "actions": [
      {
        "name": "Edit",
        "handler": "system",
        "system_op": "edit",
        "validations": [
          {
            "type": "expression",
            "name": "Open only",
            "message": "Only Open queries can be edited.",
            "expression": "{form.status} == \"O\""
          },
          {
            "type": "business_logic",
            "name": "Raiser only",
            "message": "Only the raiser can edit this query.",
            "business_logic": {
              "method": "check_query_raiser_or_mgmt",
              "description": "Raiser (or management where stated) check",
              "spec": "Return {\"error\":\"Only the raiser can edit this query.\"} unless the signed-in user's email equals RAISED_BY_EMAIL (case-insensitive) of CCW_BUSINESS_QUERY for QUERY_NO. Management is NOT allowed for Edit."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "Delete",
        "handler": "system",
        "system_op": "delete",
        "validations": [
          {
            "type": "business_logic",
            "name": "No responses; raiser or management",
            "message": "Only the raiser or management can delete a query, and only when it has no responses.",
            "business_logic": {
              "method": "check_query_deletable",
              "description": "Delete guard",
              "spec": "Return an error if any row exists in CCW_BQ_RESPONSE for the QUERY_NO ('A query with responses cannot be deleted'). Also return an error unless the signed-in user's email equals RAISED_BY_EMAIL (case-insensitive) or the user holds a management/admin role."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "Add Response",
        "handler": "message",
        "scope": "row",
        "placement": "bar",
        "capture": {
          "mode": "text",
          "prompt": "Enter your response (include how to reach you)",
          "field": "RESPONSE_TEXT"
        },
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "add_query_response",
          "description": "Add a response to the query and notify the raiser",
          "spec": "Read RESPONSE_TEXT from the payload (error if blank). Refuse with an error if CCW_BUSINESS_QUERY.STATUS for QUERY_NO is 'C' ('A closed query accepts no further responses'). Identify the responder by the signed-in user's email: allowed only if it equals RAISED_BY_EMAIL, or matches CCW_BQ_RECIPIENT.RECIPIENT_EMAIL for the QUERY_NO (case-insensitive); otherwise error 'Only recipients and the raiser can respond'. Determine RESPONDER_UNIT_NO from the matching recipient row (or RAISED_BY_UNIT_NO for the raiser); set RESPONDER_BUSINESS_NAME and RESPONDER_CONTACT_NO (CONTACT_NO_1) from CCW_MEMBER_PROFILE for that unit, or from CCW_TENANT_PROFILE (TENANT_COMPANY_NAME, CONTACT_NO_1) when the recipient is the active tenant. Insert a CCW_BQ_RESPONSE row with next LINE_NO for the QUERY_NO, RESPONSE_DATE = now. Mark the responder's CCW_BQ_RECIPIENT row VIEWED='Y'. Send an in-app notification and email to RAISED_BY_EMAIL with the response text and responder contact details. Return {\"message\":\"Response added\"}."
        },
        "validations": [
          {
            "type": "expression",
            "name": "Must be Open",
            "message": "A closed query accepts no further responses.",
            "expression": "{form.status} == \"O\""
          }
        ],
        "visible_when": "{form.status} == \"O\""
      },
      {
        "name": "Close",
        "handler": "message",
        "scope": "row",
        "capture": {
          "mode": "text",
          "prompt": "Closure remark",
          "field": "CLOSURE_REMARK"
        },
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "close_query",
          "description": "Close the query",
          "spec": "Allowed only to the raiser (signed-in email equals RAISED_BY_EMAIL, case-insensitive) or a management/admin role; otherwise error. Refuse unless STATUS='O'. Set STATUS='C', CLOSURE_REMARK from the payload, CLOSED_ON = now on CCW_BUSINESS_QUERY. Return {\"message\":\"Query closed\"}."
        },
        "validations": [
          {
            "type": "expression",
            "name": "Must be Open",
            "message": "Only Open queries can be closed.",
            "expression": "{form.status} == \"O\""
          }
        ],
        "visible_when": "{form.status} == \"O\"",
        "confirmation": {
          "mode": "reconfirm",
          "message": "Close query {form.query_no}? No further responses will be accepted."
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "Reopen",
        "handler": "message",
        "scope": "row",
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "reopen_query",
          "description": "Reopen a closed query",
          "spec": "Allowed only to the raiser (signed-in email equals RAISED_BY_EMAIL, case-insensitive) or a management/admin role; otherwise error. Refuse unless STATUS='C'. Set STATUS='O', CLOSURE_REMARK=NULL and CLOSED_ON=NULL on CCW_BUSINESS_QUERY. Return {\"message\":\"Query reopened\"}."
        },
        "validations": [
          {
            "type": "expression",
            "name": "Must be Closed",
            "message": "Only Closed queries can be reopened.",
            "expression": "{form.status} == \"C\""
          }
        ],
        "visible_when": "{form.status} == \"C\""
      },
      {
        "name": "Export",
        "handler": "system",
        "system_op": "export",
        "scope": "form",
        "export": {
          "places": [
            "list",
            "bulk",
            "record"
          ],
          "formats": [
            "xlsx",
            "csv",
            "json"
          ],
          "offer_list_view": true,
          "org_templates": true,
          "templates": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "cross_updates": [],
    "pre_commit": [
      {
        "mode": "business_logic",
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "generate_query_recipients",
          "description": "Generate recipients on first save",
          "spec": "Run only when action = 'add' (first save). From CCW_MEMBER_PROFILE where PROFILE_STATUS='A', SHOW_IN_DIRECTORY='Y' and BUSINESS_CATEGORY equals header TARGET_BUSINESS_CATEGORY, excluding UNIT_NO = header RAISED_BY_UNIT_NO, choose one recipient per unit: if OCCUPANCY_TYPE='O' (Owner Used) use the profile itself (BUSINESS_NAME, EMAIL as RECIPIENT_EMAIL); if OCCUPANCY_TYPE='R' (Given on Rent) use the tenant from CCW_TENANT_PROFILE for that UNIT_NO only when TENANT_STATUS='A', LOGIN_ENABLED='Y', SHOW_IN_DIRECTORY='Y' and the profile's SHOW_TENANT_IN_DIRECTORY='Y' and TENANT_LOGIN_ALLOWED='Y' (TENANT_COMPANY_NAME as BUSINESS_NAME, TENANT_EMAIL as RECIPIENT_EMAIL); otherwise skip the unit (a rented unit whose tenant is not shown falls back to the owner profile per the directory rule: use the owner profile). Insert rows into CCW_BQ_RECIPIENT (QUERY_NO = header QUERY_NO, LINE_NO numbered from 1, UNIT_NO, BUSINESS_NAME, RECIPIENT_EMAIL, FORWARDED_ON = now, VIEWED='N') inside the save transaction. If no recipient is found return {\"warnings\":[{\"message\":\"No businesses found in this category; the query is saved without recipients.\"}]} and still save."
        }
      }
    ],
    "post_commit": [
      {
        "mode": "business_logic",
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "notify_query_recipients",
          "description": "Email and notify recipients on first save",
          "spec": "Run only when action = 'add'. For every CCW_BQ_RECIPIENT row of the saved QUERY_NO, create an in-app notification and send an email containing SUBJECT, DESCRIPTION and the raiser's contact details (RAISED_BY_NAME, RAISED_BY_UNIT_NO, RAISED_BY_EMAIL, and the raiser's CCW_MEMBER_PROFILE.CONTACT_NO_1). Failures must not affect the save."
        }
      }
    ],
